{"seq":25,"slug":"research-methods-open-science","title":"心理学研究方法与开放科学","stage":"DONE","category":"psychology","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science","rating":{"composite":3.66,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":3.5,"positioning":3.5,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"心理学研究方法与开放科学\">心理学研究方法与开放科学</h1><p>心理学最难的不是提出关于心灵的猜想，而是判断哪一个猜想值得相信。一个人可以在咖啡馆里把任何行为讲成一个动听的故事，但要让这个故事变成可以被他人检验、推翻、复用的知识，需要一整套约束自己的工具。这个 hub 讲的就是这套工具：心理学如何把模糊的直觉变成可信的结论，又如何在二十一世纪反思自己曾经的失败。</p>\n<p>整个 hub 由四条主线串成一条递进的链。第一条线是研究设计：科学方法、四类效度、随机实验、以及当随机不可行时的相关与准实验设计，它回答的是「怎样安排观察才能让因果推断站得住」。这是全部后续讨论的方法论地基。</p>\n<p>第二条线是测量与数据：心理构念看不见摸不着，必须先变成可量化的分数，于是有了信度与效度；分数从样本中来，要推及总体就要靠抽样与统计推断；而仅有「显著」远远不够，还要问效应有多大、检验有多大把握、众多研究合起来说明什么，于是引出效应量、统计功效与元分析。这条线是一条从测量到推断的数据链，每一环的薄弱都会顺流污染最终结论。</p>\n<p>第三条线走出定量的舒适区：质性研究关心意义而非频次，混合方法与个案研究把定量定性缝合在一起，而研究伦理则是所有方法共同的底线——无论方法多严谨，伤害参与者的研究都不应被做。</p>\n<p>第四条线把前三条线推到当下的风口浪尖。复制危机暴露了 p-hacking、HARKing 等可疑研究实践如何系统性地制造假阳性；开放科学以预注册、注册报告、数据共享作为制度性的解药；而贝叶斯推断、大数据与 AI 辅助则代表了 2025 至 2026 年方法学的新前沿，连大语言模型本身也成了既是工具又是研究对象的双重存在。</p>\n<p>四条线合起来回答一个问题：心理学如何产生可信的知识，又如何在发现自己不够可信之后重建信任。建议按章顺序阅读——后面的批判只有站在前面的方法之上才看得真切。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"research-design","title":"研究设计基础","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/research-design","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"intro-and-core-concepts","title":"心理学研究方法导论","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/research-design/intro-and-core-concepts"},{"seq":2,"slug":"experimental-design","title":"实验设计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/research-design/experimental-design"},{"seq":3,"slug":"correlational-quasi-experimental","title":"非实验与相关设计","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/research-design/correlational-quasi-experimental"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"measurement-data","title":"测量与数据","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/measurement-data","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"measurement-reliability-validity","title":"测量、信度与效度","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/measurement-data/measurement-reliability-validity"},{"seq":2,"slug":"sampling-statistical-inference","title":"抽样与统计推断","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/measurement-data/sampling-statistical-inference"},{"seq":3,"slug":"effect-size-power-meta","title":"效应量、功效与元分析","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/measurement-data/effect-size-power-meta"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"qualitative-mixed-ethics","title":"质性、混合与伦理","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/qualitative-mixed-ethics","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"qualitative-methods","title":"质性研究方法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/qualitative-mixed-ethics/qualitative-methods"},{"seq":2,"slug":"mixed-methods-case-study","title":"混合方法与个案研究","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/qualitative-mixed-ethics/mixed-methods-case-study"},{"seq":3,"slug":"research-ethics","title":"研究伦理","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/qualitative-mixed-ethics/research-ethics"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"replication-open-science","title":"复制危机与开放科学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/replication-open-science","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"replication-crisis","title":"复制危机","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/replication-open-science/replication-crisis"},{"seq":2,"slug":"open-science-practices","title":"开放科学实践","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/replication-open-science/open-science-practices"},{"seq":3,"slug":"bayesian-bigdata-ai-frontiers","title":"贝叶斯、大数据与AI前沿","url":"/l-doc-books/h/psychology/research-methods-open-science/replication-open-science/bayesian-bigdata-ai-frontiers"}]}]}